 attribute group indicates the color of an element."}],"kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlbass\/step-swift.struct\/color","title":"color"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLBass/Step-swift.struct":{"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"Step"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLBass\/Step-swift.struct","title":"MXLBass.Step","kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"Step"}],"abstract":[{"text":"The bass-step type represents the pitch step of the bass of the current chord within the harmony element. The","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"text attribute indicates how the bass should appear in a score if not using the element contents.","type":"text"}],"type":"topic","role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlbass\/step-swift.struct"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL":{"type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A MusicXML parser, normalizer, validator, and formatter."}],"title":"IvorMXL","kind":"symbol","role":"collection","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLColor":{"fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MXLColor","kind":"identifier"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLColor","title":"MXLColor","kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLColor"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The color type indicates the color of an element. Color may be represented as hexadecimal RGB triples, as in"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"HTML, or as hexadecimal ARGB tuples, with the A indicating alpha of transparency. An alpha value of 00 is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"totally transparent; FF is totally opaque. If RGB is used, the A value is assumed to be FF.","type":"text"}],"type":"topic","role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlcolor"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLBass":{"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLBass"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLBass","title":"MXLBass","kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"MXLBass","kind":"identifier"}],"abstract":[{"text":"The bass type is used to indicate a bass note in popular music chord symbols, e.g. G\/C. It is generally not","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"used in functional harmony, as inversion is generally not used in pop chord symbols. As with root, it is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"divided into step and alter elements, similar to pitches. The arrangement attribute specifies where the bass","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"is displayed relative to what precedes it.","type":"text"}],"type":"topic","role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlbass"}}}